g510-linux (0.1.2) trixie; urgency=low

  * Ship linux/notify.py. The shared daemon imports notify at load time, and
    without the Linux copy that import opened macOS's own frameworks, so
    `g510 run` died before it reached the loop. sync_watcher and the three
    `g510 discord` readers now ask the new notify.AVAILABLE flag first, and
    say what cannot be read here rather than reading nothing.
  * Give linux/lcd.py the set_font() that shared code calls for `lcd.font`.
    Without it `g510 run` died in __init__ on the way to the loop, and the
    setting now reaches the panel here: a path is opened as a font file, and
    a macOS family name falls back to DejaVu, which is what _load_font
    already expected.
  * Take `reload` out from behind the keyboard gate. It reached the agent
    only when a G510 was plugged in, so with none attached every `g510`
    setting was saved and reported as applied while the agent kept running
    what it had read at boot - which is also how the beat tap gets opened
    here, where there is no keyboard to wait for.
  * Drop --no-shm from the parec call. No parec has ever had that option,
    so the beat tap exited at once on every machine and, with stderr in
    /dev/null, all that showed was a listener that heard nothing. The
    command is built in one place now, and a test holds its options
    against what `parec --help` actually offers.
  * Say what is really missing in `g510 permissions` and `g510 gui` on a
    box that has neither. No keyboard node is the board not being plugged
    in, not a permissions problem to go and fix; no display is one line
    rather than Qt's page of plugin diagnostics ending in Aborted - and it
    is asked before Qt is imported, so an ssh login does not pay for it.

 -- nikossrcs2 <taubert.philipp2@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 20:15:46 +0100

g510-linux (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=low

  * Sleep on the keyboard's evdev descriptor instead of polling it every four
    milliseconds. Measured against the hardware: 4.4% of a core down to 0.00%,
    and a G-key now wakes the agent at once rather than up to a poll later.
  * Add the Qt tray and window, reached with `g510 gui`, plus a desktop entry.
    PySide6 is a Recommends: the agent and the command line do not need it.
  * Stop calling refresh_app_color, which was a no-op on Wayland running two
    hundred and fifty times a second.

 -- Paul <paulloth2208@gmail.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 19:40:00 +0200

g510-linux (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=low

  * Initial package for the Linux port: the LCD, the G-key bindings and the
    macro recorder, on top of what hid-lg-g15 already provides.

